Start of a new crisis era
France and the rest of Europe in the focus of investors.
On Tuesday, a statistical storm low roared through Europe.
The individual states published their figures on their GDP for the 3rd quarter.
The Czech economy stagnated compared to the previous quarter, Germany and France increased.
Today, however, the obligatory market breaks all records.
Investors not only keep an eye on Spain, France, Austria and other countries.
The statistical offices of the Europazone, Germany, the Czech Republic and some other European countries published their preliminary forecasts on economic development in the third quarter.
Germany’s GDP grew by 0.5% as expected to grow by 0.4%.
Both countries simultaneously corrected their data for the second quarter, in which Germany recorded higher growth than was originally expected (growth by 0.3% instead of a predicted 0.1%), while France acknowledged a slight decline of 0.1% (original figures spoke only of stagnation).
The Czech economy grew 1.5 percent year-on-year in this year's third quarter.
Compared to the previous quarter, however, the gross domestic product stagnated and, according to Tsch, confirming the trend of slowing growth in economic performance.
Thus, the results are worse than the prognations of the analysts.
The most important events:
The Czech economy grew 1.5 percent year-on-year in this year's third quarter, but stagnated compared to the previous quarter.
According to provisional and seasonally overdicted data, the German economy grew by 0.5 percent in the third quarter.
Across the eurozone and in the EU, the economy recorded 0.2 per cent growth between July and September compared to the previous quarter, consistent with analysts' expectations.
Greece's economy shrank 5.2 percent year-on-year.
Yield from their 10-year government bonds climbed 28.45%.
The yield on Italian and Spanish government bonds rose to their critical limits.
Austria, the Netherlands, France, Belgium and other countries are also starting to feel problems...
Yield on Czech government bonds remains below 4%, even as the situation in the region deteriorates.
In Germany, voices are heard that the ECB should become the creditor of last resort.
The Czechs qualified for EURO
In Montenegro they won 1:0 and now celebrate their qualifier for 200 million
The football selection has mastered the hardest task of the whole season!
Thanks to a well-placed goalkeeper Čech and a magnificent goal from Petr Jiráček, she won 1:0 in Montenegro.
With a large dose of luck, Czech football was thus able to defend its luxurious advantage from the home game and will once again not be missing from the European Championship.
IHNED.cz followed the promotion game in a detailed reportage.
Little excitement in the first half and a huge dose of luck in the second.
The Czech selection also won quite happy 1:0 thanks to the final weakness of the home team, a brilliant Čech's and the hero of the day Jiráček in Montenegro and has thus redeemed their ticket for the European Football Championship.
Also because of the precise defensive play of the Czech team, they were only able to put more pressure on the Montenegrins in the second half.
Damjanovic and Vucinic, who scored two huge chances.
Also thanks to an excellent Petr Čech, the Czech selection will participate in the European Championships next year, it is also gratifying that a premium of about 200 million flows to domestic football.
From the first few minutes there was quite combative football played.
Both teams combined lengthily and so played mainly around the center line.
Also in the second half, the pressure of the home team was absent and the wide tees in front of the penalty area were successfully fended off by the Czech defense.
Iranian students are ready to die for their country's core program.
They formed a living shield.
A few hundred university students formed a living sign around a core object in Iran.
With this gesture, they wanted to demonstrate their support for their country's core program before a possible Israeli attack.
The students had prayed in front of the object at noon on Tuesday and subsequently announced death to the United States and Israel.
A few Hundred Students of the University in Iran's Isfahan on Tuesday formed a living sign around the core technology center in Isfahan where uranium is processed.
In doing so, they wanted to announce that they are willing to protect their country’s core program, if necessary with their own lives.
The International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) recently stated in its report that Iran has not seemed to have given up its efforts for a nuclear weapon.
There is also talk in Israel about a possible attack on Iran’s nuclear facilities.
Students had prayed at noon in front of the entrance to the complex and subsequently promulgated death to the U.S. and Israel.
In the event of an intentiful attack to largely paralyze Iran's nuclear program, according to the Israeli press, according to the Israeli press, would also be the nuclear enrichment facility in Natan's target.
The menu of a naughty child: It doesn't have breakfast and eat sausage for dinner
More than one-third of children from 9 to 13 have problems with overweight, with 9 percent of all pupils and 5 percent of all children being overweight.
Recent surveys proven - obese children mostly come from families with unhealthy lifestyles.
This shows once again how important for the healthy development of a person the milieu in which he grows up and are the examples that surround him.
On the tables of obese children, sausages are up to half more likely to be on the table than in families where normal-weighted children live.
More than 19 percent of obese children had fries for dinner on the previous day of the reconnaissance campaign under the motto "Obesity is not a coincidence".
In families with fat, sport is not exactly one of the favorite activities, which also affects the majority of today's pupils - only 15 percent replied that their parents find themselves at least once a week time for active exercise.
Survey of 900 children
The survey took place last year towards the end of the school year, with almost 900 children from elementary schools surveyed throughout the Czech Republic.
This was already the second vintage of the action "Obesity is no coincidence", which is supported by the general health insurance and the company Unilever.
So far, more than 12 thousand pupils from 4th and 8th grades have participated in the project.
Unhealthy diet and lack of exercise in the family are decisive factors that are responsible for the frighteningly increasing number of children with overweight or even obesity.
"For example, only half of the children surveyed cited eating five times a day, in the mode of breakfast-second-lunch-Vesper dinner - one of the main prerequisites for a healthy diet," according to one of the survey results.
No breakfast and sausage for dinner
Experts point out that even relative little things, such as the regular breakfast time of the family, are important for the healthy development of a child.
In the Czech Republic, however, only 23 percent of the families of pupils have breakfast.
And - in most families, everyone eats breakfast on their own.
Worst of all was the finding that in every tenth family you don't have breakfast at all.
Breakfast is the cornerstone of a healthy daily diet.
Among other things, the survey test revealed that unhealthy fries are consumed much more often in the families of overweight children.
And almost everyone - without regard to weight - drinks cute sodas (70 percent) every day
Although more than 40 percent of the children surveyed play sports, only less than half of their parents do so - only 15 percent.
Compile your own menu
Another part of the survey allowed selected children (204 boys and 172 girls from 13 schools to put together their own meal plan out of offered opportunities according to appetite and opinion.
“What Czech children between 12 and 15 prefer in terms of diet is far from the ideal of a healthy diet.
Among their favorite dishes were many pastries, meat dishes and, of course, desserts.
"Alarming is above all the great popularity of cute lemonades," is emphasized in the final report to this survey.
At lunch, i.e. the main course, pasta prevailed narrowly in front of poultry.
Legumes hardly liked the children at all and the popularity of fish and vegetable dishes as lunch was also very low.
Turning towards health
At the same time, however, the survey also showed that the children are quite willing to change their eating habits if they get correct information.
"In many cases, there has been a significant shift in the preferences towards principles of healthy diet among the control group of survey participants, who completed the questionnaire after the enlightening lecture "Obesity is not a coincidence", in many cases.
For example, this was noticeable with the sweet limos, where many children began to prioritize ordinary water.
The children also ticked poultry or fish in the questionnaire much more often as the main dish of the day and were willing to eat less dumplings or sweet food.
Professionals claim - a stylist must also be a good psychologist
In the introductory article about how stylists learn, I'd complained a bit bit that that was a bit too much stuff for starters.
I didn’t know what’s coming.
Lectures by three professionals from the industry, the clothing of problematic figures and a seminar on how the "on the pitch" runs.
It's supposed to get worse.
The closer the exam approaches, the more information and practical tasks are imminent.
But even if the course takes place every Saturday and Sunday, it is still fully occupied.
This time we debated with Director Alena (not a single man participates in the course) how to attract a woman who does not have an ideally proportioned figure.
And that's most of us, after all.
Some have too short necks, others a too boyish figure without neat curves and still others are chubby.
It is up to the stylist to visually conceal broad shoulders, prolong the neck or conjure up the necessary curves.
We also got tips on how to dress a woman type like Jennifer Lopez - i.e. with a big bosom, wide hip and narrow waist - pretty and figure-hugging, without her looking too provocative.
If, for example, the difference between the waist and the hips is so great that the skirt or pants really doesn’t fit, you should have at least one piece tailor-made tailored.
You won’t regret that, because well-fitting clothing is simply priceless.
In such a tailor-made skirt you feel much better than in one from the pole, which always slips up and slips, stands out at the waist, etc.
Boy-like figures, in turn, can allow themselves to wear clothing with wrinkles, bullies, appliqués, embroidery or gathering.
With this amount of information and figure types, I'm glad that I have a whole week to let everything go through my mind thoroughly.
And yet I'm afraid it's almost impossible in view of the applied homework.
Each of the students was assigned a celebrity, for which she should come up with suitable outfits - daywear and evening wear.
In doing so, we should take into account the current appearance, the fashion style of the corresponding star and his figure type.
I'm supposed to "attract" Miranda Kerr, whom you may know from the Victoria's Secret campaign.
Inside I cheer, because that's much better for me personally than, for for example, putting Britney Spears or Christina Aguilera, who has probably gained about a hundred kilos in recent times (well, that's a bit exaggerated), or even the young Selena Gomez.
We are supposed to cut out the garments out of magazines or search, print them on the Internet and then edit them graphically.
In the "Moodboard", as the whole result is called, our very personal style and our relationship to graphic design should be expressed.
Because it is very important to also think about the graphic side of styling.
The stylist not only attracts the models purely physically, but also designs the so-called product page in the journals (according to the specific specifications, for example trend handbags, coats, etc.).
The stylist and designer Mario Kameník told us about this.
But it wasn't until Sunday.
This means a stylist must have a good overall overview.
The Saturday lecture, which was filled with information about figure types, was immediately seasoned by three visitors from the industry:
by stylist Jan Pokorný, fashion designer Jakub Polanka and fashion photographer Ben Renč.
Jakub reminded us that fashion is an illusion that a stylist should be able to take advantage.
And sent-in stylist can work with a single piece of clothing in very different ways.
The magic word is variability.
For example, you can wear a trench coat as usual over the jeans, i.e. like a T-shirt or coat, but you can also wear it on your nude body, put on your heels and wear it as a dress.
It is enough to roll up the sleeves or the collar and the whole look looks very different.
"Play with it," he insisted.
But the following advice came to me: "First you have to know the rules perfectly."
"Only then are you allowed to hurt them," Jakub said.
I finally realize why we have to timpanize all these doctrines, what you can combine with what and why, even if you often get to see completely different things in fashion journals.
Not to mention fashion shows.
Thanks to the photographer Ben, I now know that a stylist must have prepared a lot more clothing variants than he ultimately photographs.
So you have to be prepared to style at least fifteen for a fashion story with ten pages (i.e. ten outfits).
And also that the clothing on the photo in combination with other accessories sometimes looks very different than in reality.
So you have to reckon with all of this when designing the outfit.
Jan Pokorný also confirmed that image and style sometimes make up half of the success.
All you have to do is look at Madonna, a not exactly brilliant singer who made image and marketing into a world star.
In the Czech Republic, the services of a stylist are rather reserved.
Even well-known personalities often consider this to be thrown-out money (the main thing is that I bring something that I look like is secondary).
And if one of us can already be styled, then we should expect that he or she will almost certainly impose a completely different (smaller) size than he or she really needs.
Then you only need to google to find with certainty that the tabloid press writes that the corresponding celebrity has returned to or decreased, etc.
Jan and Mario urged us on Sunday not to believe that a stylist only needs to focus on fashion and then "assemble" the outfit.
In his work, above all, he has to communicate with the people he styles and he has to be a clever psychologist.
Assessing people without improving and standing by their opinion.
"If any manager orders us to sift through her wardrobe and add pretty pieces, then we can't clear out the whole cupboard and tell her - my God, that's terrible."
"You have to find at least some commendable things that you're recommending what you can wear," says Mario.
He also showed us very concretely what such a so-called "place bag" must include.
So such a bag, which can be buttoned up at the waist and in which you carry all the necessary proprieties.
In addition to such clear things as scissors, dispensers for hair removal or safety pins, it also contains such utensils as a nylon thread (thus the stylist helps to photograph products, such as handbags or hats), special clips with which the clothes are gathered on the back, if it is too large (pins or other clamps are prohibited, so that the fabric does not break) and, of course.
However, so that we not only have to listen, but can also try something practically, we learned how to glue shoes properly.
Even when photographing in the studio, where the floor is level, you can damage the sole of the shoe, let alone the outside.
We glued and glued ourselves...
With scissors you must not even touch the shoes, so that you do not damage them.
So you have to be really skillful.
Mario delighted me by praising my "creation" without restrictions.
The skills mentioned aren’t exactly my strength.
All of this was just a fraction of what we heard on the second weekend sequel course.
In the meantime, one thing has become clear to me - dedicating oneself to styling at a professional level is not child's play.
V Need for Speed: "The Run" - The Illegal Race Across America
Review
The originally carefree ride becomes a series of completely avoidable, dilettante errors to the routine journey to the early shift.
It was possible to fulfill the ambitions to a large extent, but what’s the use if obviously no one wanted to do a bit more.
Even before he got to the counter, the new part with the subtitled "The Run" aroused high expectations.
After all, he promised to move the years-old game series "Need for Speed" back into a new dimension and in the playable demonstration examples, he actually did not seem to be just one of many action racing games.
We were also curious as to how the fitted passages, in which the main protagonist gets out of the car and continues on foot.
But as you’re used to NFS, it’s ultimately a lot different than you’d expected.
Sure - potentially it's quite decent arcade races, but overall the game is diminished by some superfluous flaws that have been more or less present in this series for a few years.
So it's actually no longer mistakes, but rather signs of an incomprehensible laziness of the game developers.
The adventure begins very well.
For the first time one is introduced into history, whose main character Jack has certain problems of personal character; the only solution seems to be to participate in an illegal race across America.
In San Francisco, i.e. on the West Coast, you sit at the steering wheel - with the task of being the first in New York.
The basic idea contains a number of interesting elements.
The entire route is divided into ten stages and into more than fifty individual races.
This means that each race is held on a different track and that the individual stages take place in a different, sufficiently different and interesting environment.
You don't get the impression that game would offer the same again and again.
Some environments are still extremely pretty to look at, although the technical level of the graphics does not go beyond that of the earlier parts of the series.
So nothing earth-shattering.
But the drive through the desert, through autumnal scenery or high up through deeply snow-covered scenery is visually very pleasant.
Every now and then, untypical elements bring a bit of variety to the individual races.
In the desert, for example, you are surprised by a desert storm that severely restricts visibility.
In the mountains, in turn, you have to make sure that you are not spilled by an avalanche.
By the way, the individual races are installed quite well in succession.
It's only a few, but they're enough.
For a while you try to overtake the prescribed number of opponents (in principle a classic race), then you have time to catch up (classic race against the stopwatch), then a personal duel with a single opponent awaits.
And in addition, the police interfere, which wants to screw up the whole thing.
A novelty are passages in which Jack leaves the car.
It’s more about certain interactive animations in which Jack escapes from someone and where the player has to help him by pressing the right button at the right moment.
So nothing complicated.
Surprisingly, however, there are far fewer such passages in the game than one would expect (specifically probably only three).
Ultimately, this is rather to the advantage of the matter, because at least this element has no chance to become boring - it belongs in the context of the above to the elements that make the game more varied.
The driving model progresses in the footsteps of the preceding parts.
That is, from today's point of view, it doesn't rip out trees, on the other hand you couldn't say it's bad.
If you are looking for realistic simulations, you have to look elsewhere.
But an action-packed racing, the local driving model continues to do justice quite well, although you could find better in the competition.
Until then, so far everything is in good order.
True problems don't arise until after a certain amount of time.
In contrast to the driving model, the Collision model isn't quite O.K.
It’s hard to be expected to calculate complicated deformations and collisions, but if you don’t know how the car behaves before any impact on any object, it’s obviously not all right.
Typical example: When driving closely overtaking or driving past oncoming cars, in some places the other car "roam" the other car only easily, but in other, almost identical situation you get into a slingshot and turn wild piroutets.
Or drives the cart straight to junk.
Thanks to the restart system, this doesn’t matter anymore, it’s always annoying.
The restarts are solved like this: if you have total damage or land far off the track, then the game throws you back to the last indication of the track.
Only - in every race you only have five restarts.
If you have exhausted them, everything starts all over again..
So the restarts are more like an aid, in case something doesn't succeed, but you shouldn't rely on it.
Sometimes, however, the restart doesn’t even help, it doesn’t help but learn the critical section from your head.
What’s very uncomfortable is that the same things often happen in the same places.
For example, some curves you have to drive through in a very specific way, otherwise you just don’t fit through.
Elsewhere you always encounter "civilan" cars in the same configuration at the appropriate location, regardless of whether you're the first or fifth, five seconds earlier or a minute later.
This is particularly annoying in situations, when you see that the opponent gets past two oncoming cars in front of one, but until you get there yourself, the cars are already in such a position that you have to bypass or brake them.
And it doesn’t matter when you get there, because it’s all designed in such a way that this situation is always close to your nose.
The opponents have other advantages.
In the whole game there are a few places where you are always overtaken at the same place by the same opponent and here again without regard to the time.
What's craziest at the conclusion of the game on the long bridge you'll pass in the opposite direction.
The opponent obviously has to overtake a devil coming out.
And then if he's in front of one, then of course he takes the view, so that you initially drive your own car a few times in Klump.
Sure - you just want to make the game more exciting and more exciting but this intention is so clear that it quickly spoils the joy of the game.
And that's a pity, because despite a simpler driving model, the game is overall quite entertaining and in some places so action-packed that you almost don't know where your head stands.
And in principle it doesn't matter what "it's to blame" - the concept with fifty unique routes, the arrangement of the races in a way that no boredom can arise, or something completely different...
An unusual idea is also the change of cars in the course of the races.
You must not overlook the gas stations on the track, because it is precisely here that you can change the car, although in most cases the car that you have is enough.
The cars are divided into three categories.
The sports cars are well suited for the urban areas, the strong American sedans for the straight highways and exotic super sports cars for the technical rides, for example on the serpentines in the mountains.
Hand in hand with the mode of the game's history also goes the task mode (challenges) - i.e. the races in the individual localities known from history.
There are not only medals here, but also to win experience points for one's own profile, which is together for tasks (challenges) and history.
To get to the higher driver level, various items need to be unlocked: from the car, up to the backgrounds for the profile.
This is at the same time associated with the online function Autolog, which, among other things, compares its own results with those of other players and also ensures further collective functions.
One of other incomprehensible carvers is a situation in the last race of history.
Here you come by car to a subway tunnel (my way), where in the dark on the rails you carse long (my way).
On the speedometer, digits look between 150 a 200 km/h (my way), but there suddenly comes a subway from behind and uncompromisingly to scrap.
In our editorial office we will probably argue for a long time about whether this was a blackout of the game designers or whether the authors consider us so stupid.
The technical side is nothing overwhelming, but at least the overall visual impression is quite appealing in most cases and even brilliant here and there.
It is all the more annoying that at some exciting moments the refresh rate slows down and this is sometimes quite dramatic.
However, this applies in particular to accidents with a greater number of participants, where a continuous FPS is of no use anyway.
The tone reproduction is so far O.K. and the soundtrack is a matter of taste.
In an effort to appeal to such a widle and only possible scale of rather young audiences, a soundtrack a lá "from everyone" emerged - but who buys such a game because of the music?!
Need for Speed: The Run? The feelings are rather mixed.
If the game weren't diminished by the mentioned totally unnecessarious errors, we could have maintained with the breast tone of belief that The Run is the best piece of NFS in recent years.
But that's how the game seems somehow unfinished.
It’s a great pleasure for yourself, but you should be prepared for these mistakes with the power of airport headlights.
Concert of the "Students of the Velvet Revolution" with singing ensembles of the Charles University
For the third time, the Festa Academica Festival now offers for the third time the combination of World Students’ Day with the Anniversary of the Velvet Revolution and this with a musical experience.
In the course of the festival, there will be twent to book part and university choirs.
The focus of the festival is the two concerts, which take place on 17 November.
“Karlsuniversität has a large share in the festival.”
"Among the participants, the choir of the Faculty of Pedagogy and the Faculty of Humanistic Studies are also represented and the festival committee also includes Rector Václav Hampl," said Jakub Čaloun.
An absolute highlight of the festival is the public concert of technical school choirs, which takes place on November 17 from 2 p.m. in the square in front of the National Technical Library in Dejvice.
On the program is the composition of the important Czech jazzer Karel Růžička "Celebration Jazz Mass".
In the evening hours, the concert "Students of the Velvet Revolution" (Studenty sametu) takes place in the gala rooms of the Volkshaus in Vinohrady, in which also university choirs, choirs of the Charles University not excluded.
Festa Academica’s goal not only to celebrate World Students’ Day worthy and commemorate the 22nd Anniversary of the Velvet Revolution, but to present choral music to the public at the highest level and to promote the creative cooperation of young people.
The main organizer is the association of Czech choirs in cooperation with the Johannes-Kepler-Gymnasium.
Bohuslav Svoboda, the mayor of the capital Prague and Václav Hampl, the rector of Charlemagne University, took over the entire event.
The festival will take place from November 16 to 20 in Prague and Pardubice.
In addition to festive concerts, the schedule also includes numerous music gatherings, student happanings, matinees and other events.
Interested parties can find detailed information on the websites of the festival www.festaacademica.cz
EU Ambassador Vicenová:
The Czeches have the reputation of negativists and Eurosceptics
"The Treaty of Lisbon has palpablimately undermined the balance among individual institutions."
I didn't expect such a hard war.'
"It will take five or six years for the waves to become smooth and everyone get used to their new role," Milena Vicenová, the Czech ambassador to the European Union, began her lecture at the Faculty of Law.
In the first part of her lecture, in which she managed to describe the individual organs of the EU and their mutual relations in such a manageable and comprehensible way that she could have envoyed many lecturers of the Faculty of Law of the Charles University.
Ms Vicenová also praised the new Permanent Chairman of the Council of Europe Herman Van Rompuy:
“Initially, there was criticism that he was too inconspicuous – a grey civil servant who couldn’t cope with such a role, but I have to say it took everyone’s breath away with how well he has embraced the matter.
“He is a person who manages to listen patiently to twenty-seven member states, to communicate with them and who, above all, has clear ideas of how to proceed with the EU.
She then explained the new position of the High Representative for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy in response to the question: Who actually is this - the European Union? Which number should I call?", i.e. as an important step towards the unification and better readability of EU policy towards states, such as China or India.
No one wants to ban us our oil humic
Ms Vicenová also devoted herself to the agenda according to which the European Union lived, lives and intends to live in the near future.
She described the Czech presidency of two years ago as a success.
The Czechs had mastered the financial crisis and the gas crisis and also hosted the Eastern Partnership Summit.
She described the case of the government during the presidency as a major negative, which had severely harmed the image of the Czech Republic.
The Czech Representation in the EU currently has its hands full.
In the words of the ambassador, it was not only with the presidency, but also with the subsequent crisis, which has not yet been overcome to this day.
And the EU's seven-year budget has yet to be approved, which makes things much more complicated precisely because of today's economic situation.
Whether it becomes a lean and economical budget, which economic sectors are given priority, which countries are being supported more and which are less supported - all this is now on the agenda.
The ambassador also recalls her own slogans with which she came to Brussels: "Understandably about Europe."
“If I don’t like something, it’s gruesomy abbreviations, foreign words and jargon that nobody understands.
As a citizen, how am I supposed to know whether you are really crooked or round cucumbers and bananas of different sizes in Brussels, or whether someone actually wants to forbid us the Quargel.
She would also have liked to use the EU's soil to get more Czechs into European institutions.
Europe of two or different speeds in prospect
According to the EU ambassador, the Czechs have a reputation for being Euroscepticians who perceive more the negatives than the positive sides of the cause.
All the more annoying is the weak representation of Czeches in European institutions.
Many factors are to blame for this, including the reluctance of our candidates, their inability to write motivation letters and, last but not least, the weak support of the Czech side.
In addition to the successful Czech Presidency, it also highlighted the strength and cooperation of the Visegrad Group, so-called V4.
"Believe me, if a pole or Hungarian comes to me and a Slovak is nearby, then the Frenchman next to me means: "Hey, what do you put your heads together - isn't that your V4 again?" and in the process makes a pretty sour face.
According to Ms Vicenové, the EU mainly expects tough rules for Member States' budget policy in the future.
She sees the concept of a Europe of two or even different speeds as much more real, as a "European Federation".
“We here have the countries of the eurozone and the countries away from the eurozone.
“We have the Schengen area and we already have the institute of strengthened cooperation.”
“For the first time it has been said that only those countries that want it to work together and those who don’t want it are supposed to stand quietly away.”
"There will be more and more such institutions, which ultimately boils down to a strong "Europe of different speeds," Ms Vicenová expects.
In this regard, it also acknowledged the role of the Czech Republic and Herman Van Rompuyes in enforcing the principle, according to which all issues with an impact on the entire EU must be discussed by all Member States, and not only by eurozone countries.
Brand story:
Innovator IBM enters the second century of its existence
If you wanted to look for a suitable word that characterizes IBM's strategy most accurately, then this would probably be the word "longibility."
For the general public, IMB is synonymous with technological revolution, it is known as a modern company, although a century has elapsed since its inception.
The basis for this longevity was already laid by its first boss - the visionary Thomas J. Watson sen.
Already he represented the slogan that countless worldwide problems could be easily solved if people were willing to think a bit.
His slogan "Think!" thus became the hallmark around which the life of the future giant should play out (and at the same time the title of the company's in-house magazine, which was published by IBM in 1935).
This was also the basis of Watsen’s thoroughly prepared corporate culture.
“For us from IBM, this long-term thinking means a continual movement towards the future.
IBM survived and was also successful for an entire century because it has remained true to its principles and didn’t shy away from changing everything else.
This allowed us, in the course of our first century, to transform the technologies, the business and also society.
We hope to create even more over the next hundred years," said Samuel J. Palmisano, today's director of the company on the occasion of the anniversary.
Well-thought-out system
Already in the thirties, Watson operated social care of its employees - in a similar way to the entrepreneur Baťa in Czechoslovakia: The IBM people were one of the first American employees to have paid leave, insurance by the entrepreneur plus elegant uniforms as workwear and a well-thought-out remuneration system for the best innovators and retailers.
IBM’s long-term relationships with their customers are just as sophisticated.
From the very beginning, the company was ingenious in the promotion of talent - as one of the first companies in the world, IBM lifted any discrimination - and was able to choose accordingly.
In line with this anti-discrimination strategy is also the current plan that Palmisan, at the helm of IMB, will be alternated by a woman next year - by Virginia Rometty.
She has been with IBM for thirty years and has held the position of head of sales, marketing and strategy.
In recent years, IBM has made so-called online brainstormings, from which many future strategies and innovations arise.
No wonder - there are enough ideas, almost half a million people are employed in the company.
An institution with a good reputation
Their unwavering position in the business guarantees the company a strong image and this both internally and externally.
"From the very beginning, IMB had the concept of an institution rather than a mere technology company," Economist told Harvard Business School professor and the author of a book about IBM, Rosabeth Moss Kanter.
"IBM is not a technology company, but a company that helps solve business problems using technologies," added George Colony of consulting firm Forrester Research.
As the company itself points out, there is a difference to only be present in the market or shape it directly through this presence.
IMB - nicknamed "Big Blue" in the states of its logo because of family, has grown into one of the world's largest corporations in a century.
It's one of the most versatile technology companies ever - IBM develops hardware and software, infrastructures, hosting, and consulting services in an incredible product breadth - from servers to nanotechnology.
Of all American technology companies, IBM owns the most patents and five of its employees have already been awarded the Nobel Prize.
His most well-known inventions include, for example, ATMs, credit cards, financial swaps, barcodes or even the floppy.
With approximately $220 billion in stock market value (market capitalization), IBM was the second-largest technology company (equal to Apple) this year, overtaking Microsoft for the first time since 1996.
Looking Ahead
Not all products and innovations met the tastes of today's customers - unhappy were, for example, the attempt with their own OS/2 operating system, the online service Prodigy or the computers IBM PC jr.
"Business is based on the forward movement, so you mustn't emotionally bind to the past," says Samuel J. Palmisano.
That's why IBM doesn't have a problem building its foundations on different platforms - and if they don't work to leave them again.
In contrast to opponent Microsoft, which in principle stands and falls with its Windows operating system.
Promising Technologies
IBM's gains contribute to the largest degree of services, software and hardware are one-fifth each.
In 1990, hardware with a more than fifty percent share was still the most represented.
Since 2000, IBM has sold $15 billion worth of low-profit assets, but in the same period it invested € $58 billion in purchasing promising technologies.
In these investments, IBM continues even after 2008, when the modern-day financial crisis swept across the world for the first time like a storm.
Here, too, IBM remained true to the legacy of its first boss Thomas J. Watson, who, in the midst of the great global economic crisis, increased its scope of investment.
So far, it seems that IBM will survive today's crisis unscathed.
The value of IMB shares has increased rocket-like 120 percent since 2008 and the company’s net profit is growing continually.
IBM's corporate slogan is that everything can be changed - just the values don't.
For this reason, too, it can be expected that this flexible giant will also overcome the next crisis.
IMB history: From cheese slicer to world flights
Established one hundred years agove in New York (IMB (International Business Machines), IBM (International Business Machines) initially had a rather complicated name - Computing Tabulating Recording Corporation.
She took over the name IBM only in 1924 - originally it was about a brand designation for a branch in Canada and South America.
The foundation for the later company IB was the merger of four companies, whose history dates back to the 80s of the 19th century.
They possessed technologies such as, for example, the famous cutting card clocks for registeringing the beginning and end of work.
Charles Ranlett Flint became the architect of this new company, who also chaired the Supervisory Board until 1930.
And it was Flint who hired the chief executive of competitor Thomas J. Wanst to help him manage the company.
This leader then even dwarfed IBM's founders - Watson's ideas to this day base the company's invincible culture and identity.
Watson ran the company until 1952.
IMB, as the name suggests, began manufacturing and distributing all possible machines for the trade - from sausage and cheese cutters, to cash registers.
In the first four decades that Watson ran the firm, he doubled its sales to $9 million and the company gradually expanded to all continents.
Watson was so indispensable for the company that he sat in the executive chair for a whole for forty years, only then he was replaced by his son, Thomas Watson Junior.
Under his leadership, IBM began to work on the development of artificial intelligence and also developed the first programming language.
In the 1960s, technicians and computers from IMB helped NASA to direct flights into space - to Mercury and Saturn and, in 1969, also the famous flight of humans to the moon.
Meanwhile, in 1964, IMB developed the first family of computers with the same computer architecture - the IBM System/360 series.
A classic PC, which determined the computer standard of that time, was launched in 1981 under the name IMBM 5150.
Twenty years later, IBM sold its computational production to the Chinese company Lenovo, on the other hand it bought the consultant portion of PricewaterhouseCoopers and thus fully entered the business of consulting services and services with high added value.
The strategy IBM pays for itself over the past three years is the "Smarter Planet" concept.
It embodies the intention to use technologies wisely in areas that have not even been envisaged, e.g. to improve the situation in transport and urban administration.
In the retail sector, IBM recently introduced the "Smarter Commerce" platform designed to help traders guide the entire commercial cycle.
IBM also has a strong history in the Czech Republic.
As early as 1932, IBB established a branch in what was then Czechoslovakia - the first country in Central and Eastern Europe.
Today IBM ČR also operates a strategic outsourcing center in Brno.
The Headquarters for Central and Eastern Europe is located in Prague and there is also a top research team of world-level researchers, which deals with the technology of voice recognition.
Darina Rychtářová on her unfaithful husband:
Iveta - you can keep this donkey, I don't want it anymore!
Darina Rychtářová (53) says - now it's over!
After her spouse Josef Rychtář (53) from the protector of Iveta Bartošová (45) had become her lover, Darina still remained the hope that Joseph would awaken from his pink dream and come home.
But now it's finally over with the patience and for further life she has set herself clear rules.
"Josef can come home, but nothing more than my partner," explained D. Rychtářová.
When Darina Rychtářová had offered shelter to the singer I. Bartošová in her own house, she probably wouldn’t even have dreamed how it would end with her husband.
When Iveta moved out and back to Říčany after 30 days at her insistence, Joseph immediately went along.
Yes, he even publicly confessed that he loves them.
Over time, Darina resigned, indeed it even seemed as if she wanted to reconcile with her unfaithful husband - now, however, she finally gave him the running pass.
Rychytář doesn't care who his wife sleeps with
If Rychtář Ivetta Bartošová were to leave in the future, he will certainly not welcome open arms at home.
"He is the biological father of my dreams, and if he wants to decide his days in our common home, I will not chase him out."
"However, not as a beloved, lost old donkey, but as a person to whom I still have certain ties," Ms Rychtářová revealed; but she also said that she had already emotionally separated from him and insisted solely on mutual decency.
Josef has so far carried the circumstance that Darina has locked his back door with dignity.
"I respect my wife's decision."
“I’m staying with Iveta, that doesn’t change.”
“My wife wants a paper marriage and I respect that.”
"The company keeps running, I'll take care of the repairs, the garden, the property, I'll do the purchases."
"With Darina I talk quite normally, but we don't share the bed," said J. Rychtář (the sheet) Blesk.
If Darina wants to find a new love, he doesn’t want to stop it.
“We don’t sleep with each other, so I don’t care if she has a boyfriend or who that is.
It is clear to me that this is my fault, I fell in love with Iveta and that is why I take any responsibility.
The worst female intuitions: what about you?
If you ask the men to name some typical female unbatches, they invariably shake some out of their sleeves.
Dear women, do you recognize yourself in the following lines, in which we review a few immoralities, which let the men's blood in the veins?
Purchasing addiction
Does her husband accuse them of being addicted to shopping?
Do you have to buy yourself at least one Hader weekly?
Do you like to go shopping and can it also be a bit more with promotions?
In your case, it’s really about a weakness.
Some women are at least aware of this and try to keep their lust for shopping under control.
But hand on heart, which woman can stand to stroll through a clothes store in search of a well-fitted outerwear and not to try out all (in all sorts of color combinations) in the cabin?
Even though shopping is a hobby for most women, it is often pure hell for men.
Consider how many times you've said to her husband - stay out often...
Constant dissatisfaction
“Am I not too fat?”
"I'd have to lose at least five kilos - should I start jogging or doing gymnastics?"
“Do you even like it?”
Does this seem familiar to them?
Yeah?
Then you're probably one of the women who's obsessed with what they look like.
This doesn’t mean you’re supposed to let go, but many men are allergic if their wife is constantly whining about her appearance.
The stronger gender agrees - with increasing frequency of complaints, women are increasingly incompatible.
Order and cleanliness first
It's a fight against windmills.
Cleaning windows, wiping tiles and dust, chafing the tub - and at least twice a week.
Do you scold your partner because he tramples on the clean tiles again with dirty shoes, do you scold the children, because the justed sink is dirty again and because the glass door on the living room cabinet already has fingerprints again, when polishing makes so much effort?
If you suffer from this kind of "deviance", then you should know that you must not exaggerate anything and that order and cleanliness do not come first in family life.
Ultimately, this immeasurable purification can also harm mutual relations and, above all, rest in the family.
Stitches
"Dirty gym pants come into the laundry basket."
“Are you really going to wear those old socks tomorrow?”
"You don't just throw a wet towel on the floor."
If your partner is exposed to such a tirade, don’t be surprised that this puts him on the palm.
Clearly, this isn’t bad, they just want that everything has its order.
If the men knew this, then the women might not need to complain so much.
Gossip and gossip
Some women like to clap and gossip, there is whispering behind their backs or even slandered or one forges covenants.
Women are focused on relationships, that’s why they like to pant through such topics, for example – who, where, with whom, how and why.
Arguably each of us women has a bit harmless gossip and gossip in stock.
Hand on heat - that's probably peculiar to all women.
However, this is not to be confused with gossip aunts of gross calibre, to whom nothing and no one is sacred, who probably despise everyone in their environment and who pose a considerable danger, especially for women's collectives.
